    "id": "273249d863d5",
    "cat": "finance",
    "title_en": "America Movil's Claro open to further acquisitions in Brazil after Desktop deal",
    "title_zh": "在完成 Desktop 收購案後，America Movil 旗下的 Claro 對在巴西進行進一步收購持開放態度",
    "title_zcn": "在完成Desktop交易后，America Movil旗下的Claro表示愿意在巴西进行进一步收购",
    "title_ja": "アメリカ・モビル傘下のクラロ、デスクトップ買収を受け、ブラジルでのさらなる買収に前向き",
    "title_ko": "아메리카 모빌의 클라로, 데스크톱 인수 이후 브라질 내 추가 인수에 개방적",
    "s_en": "SAO PAULO, April 23 (Reuters) - Telecom operator Claro, owned by Mexico's America Movil, is ‌open to new deals in Brazil following ‌its recently announced purchase of internet provider Desktop.\n\"We an",
    "s_zh": "聖保羅，4月23日（路透社）— 隸屬於墨西哥America Movil集團的電信營運商Claro，在近期宣布收購網路服務供應商Desktop後，表示對在巴西展開新交易持開放態度。\n「我們",
    "s_zcn": "圣保罗4月23日（路透社）——隶属于墨西哥America Movil集团的电信运营商Claro在近期宣布收购互联网服务提供商Desktop后，表示愿意在巴西寻求新的合作机会。\n“我们",
    "s_ja": "【サンパウロ】4月23日（ロイター） - メキシコのアメリカ・モビル傘下の通信事業者クラロは、先日発表したインターネットプロバイダー「デスクトップ」の買収を受け、ブラジルでの新たな取引に前向きな姿勢を示している。\n「我々は",
    "s_ko": "상파울루, 4월 23일 (로이터) - 멕시코의 아메리카 모빌(America Movil)이 소유한 통신사 클라로(Claro)는 최근 인터넷 서비스 제공업체 데스크톱(Desktop) 인수를 발표한 데 이어 브라질 내 새로운 거래에 개방적인 입장을 보이고 있다.\n\"우리는",
    "so": "yahoo.finance",
    "url": "https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/america-movils-claro-open-further-153602084.html",
    "time": "2026-04-23T15:36:02+00:00",
    "rank": 1776958562.0,
    "content": "SAO PAULO, April 23 (Reuters) - Telecom operator Claro, owned by Mexico's America Movil, is ‌open to new deals in Brazil following ‌its recently announced purchase of internet provider Desktop.\n\"We analyze all ​the options that come our way,\" Claro's Brazil CEO Rodrigo Marques told reporters in Sao Paulo on Thursday. \"But we don't buy just anything for the ‌sake of buying. ⁠It has to be related to our customers' needs.\"\nClaro announced last month a ⁠deal to buy a 73% stake in Desktop for an enterprise value of 4 billion reais ($808.93 ​million), with ​a base equity ​price of about 2.4 ‌billion reais after deducting the Brazilian firm's net debt.\nMarques noted that the deal still requires approval from antitrust watchdog CADE and telecom regulator Anatel, which he expects could be granted by the ‌end of the year.\nThe executive ​said the Desktop acquisition was ​driven by the ​company's strong presence in Sao Paulo ‌state, Brazil's most populous ​and economically significant, ​while noting that Claro is open to deals across the country as it operates ​nationwide.\nAmerica Movil is ‌controlled by the family of Mexican billionaire ​Carlos Slim.\n($1 = 4.9448 reais)\n(Reporting by Luciana Magalhaes; ​Editing by Gabriel Araujo)",
    "content_source": "full"
  },
