    "id": "0c2718b3b66b",
    "cat": "finance",
    "title_en": "Is PayPal Holdings, Inc. (PYPL) A Good Stock To Buy Now?",
    "title_zh": "PayPal Holdings, Inc. (PYPL) 現在是值得買進的好股票嗎？",
    "title_zcn": "PayPal Holdings, Inc. (PYPL) 现在是值得买入的好股票吗？",
    "title_ja": "PayPal Holdings, Inc.（PYPL）は、今買うべき銘柄なのか？",
    "title_ko": "PayPal Holdings, Inc. (PYPL)는 지금 매수하기 좋은 주식인가?",
    "s_en": "Is PYPL a good stock to buy?\nWe came across a\nbullish thesis\non PayPal Holdings, Inc. on William’s Substack by William Fleming-Daniels. In this article, we will summarize the bulls’ thesis on PYPL. Pa",
    "s_zh": "PYPL 是一支值得買進的股票嗎？\n我們在 William Fleming-Daniels 的 William’s Substack 上看到一篇關於 PayPal Holdings, Inc. 的\n看漲論點\n。本文將針對 PYPL 總結多頭的觀點。",
    "s_zcn": "PYPL 是一只值得买入的股票吗？\n我们在威廉·弗莱明-丹尼尔斯（William Fleming-Daniels）的 Substack 专栏中看到了一篇关于 PayPal Holdings, Inc. 的\n看涨论点\n。本文将总结多头对 PYPL 的看涨论点。",
    "s_ja": "PYPLは買いの銘柄でしょうか？\nウィリアム・フレミング＝ダニエルズ氏が運営する「William’s Substack」で、PayPal Holdings, Inc.に関する\n強気の見解\nを見つけました。本記事では、PYPLに対する強気派の見解を要約します。Pa",
    "s_ko": "PYPL은 매수할 만한 주식일까요?\n우리는 윌리엄 플레밍-다니엘스(William Fleming-Daniels)가 윌리엄스 서브스택(William’s Substack)에 게시한 페이팔 홀딩스(PayPal Holdings, Inc.)에 대한\n낙관적 전망\n을 접했습니다. 이 글에서는 PYPL에 대한 낙관론자들의 주장을 요약해 보겠습니다. Pa",
    "so": "yahoo.finance",
    "url": "https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/paypal-holdings-inc-pypl-good-153200221.html",
    "time": "2026-04-23T15:32:00+00:00",
    "rank": 1776958320.0,
    "content": "Is PYPL a good stock to buy?\nWe came across a\nbullish thesis\non PayPal Holdings, Inc. on William’s Substack by William Fleming-Daniels. In this article, we will summarize the bulls’ thesis on PYPL. PayPal Holdings, Inc.'s share was trading at $51.22 as of April 22\nnd\n. PYPL’s trailing and forward P/E were 9.47 and 9.68 respectively according to Yahoo Finance.\nPayPal (PYPL) Stock Down Significantly After Jim Cramer Advised Careful Buying\nPayPal Holdings, Inc. operates a technology platform that enables digital payments for merchants and consumers worldwide. PYPL is a mispriced global payments leader down 78% from its peak, processing $1.8 trillion in annual volume, serving 439 million accounts, and generating over $6 billion in free cash flow. It trades at about 8x earnings and a 14% free cash flow yield, implying distressed valuation despite 45% online payments share and platform-scale economics.\nRead More:\n15 AI Stocks That Are Quietly Making Investors Rich\nRead More:\nUndervalued AI Stock Poised For Massive Gains: 10000% Upside Potential\nNew CEO Enrique Lores is tasked with restoring execution, stabilizing branded checkout growth, and improving product velocity amid competition from Apple Pay, Google Pay, and Stripe. Venmo is growing over 20% annually, BNPL exceeds $40 billion in volume, and unbranded processing continues double-digit expansion. Fastlane and AI-driven agentic commerce initiatives, including Cymbio, aim to embed PayPal into future AI shopping workflows.\nThe company generates resilient cash flows supporting $6 billion in annual buybacks at an ~11–12% yield, enhancing per-share value even in low growth. Operating margins remain stable near the high teens, with multiple rerating drivers including Venmo monetization, BNPL scaling, and checkout stabilization. Even conservative valuation models suggest upside toward $70–$100 per share, supported by strong free cash flow generation and buybacks.\nThe market prices PayPal as a declining asset, but fundamentals reflect a durable, cash-generative platform with multiple optionality layers. With strong buyback intensity, potential AI commerce optionality, and improving execution under new leadership, PayPal offers asymmetric upside as market skepticism remains elevated despite stable cash generation and diversified growth engines across payments, credit, and digital wallets, positioning it as a contrarian compounder with rerating potential over the next 12–24 months.\nPreviously, we covered a\nbullish thesis\non PayPal Holdings, Inc. (PYPL) by William Fleming-Daniels in May 2025, which highlighted its mispriced valuation, strong free cash flow generation, buyback-driven upside, and AI commerce optionality. PYPL’s stock price has depreciated by approximately 22.76% since our coverage. Fleming-Daniels reinforces a similar bullish view, emphasizing execution-led growth across Venmo, BNPL, and Fastlane expansion.",
    "content_source": "full"
  },
