    "title_en": "Knight-Swift says shippers already seeking peak-season capacity",
    "title_zh": "Knight-Swift 表示，貨主們已開始尋求旺季的運輸運力",
    "title_zcn": "Knight-Swift表示，货主们已经在为旺季寻求运力",
    "title_ja": "ナイト・スウィフト社によると、荷主はすでに繁忙期の輸送能力を確保しようとしている",
    "title_ko": "나이트-스위프트는 화주들이 이미 성수기 운송 능력을 확보하기 위해 움직이고 있다고 밝혔다",
    "s_en": "Knight-Swift Transportation anticipates significant contractual rate hikes during the current and upcoming bid cycles as the freight market emerges from a nearly four-year downturn. Strict regulatory ",
    "s_zh": "隨著貨運市場從長達近四年的低迷期中復甦，Knight-Swift Transportation 預期在當前及未來的投標週期中，合約運費將大幅上調。嚴格的監管",
    "s_zcn": "随着货运市场走出长达近四年的低迷期，Knight-Swift Transportation预计在当前及未来的投标周期中，合同运费将出现大幅上涨。严格的监管",
    "s_ja": "ナイト・スウィフト・トランスポーテーションは、貨物市場が4年近くに及ぶ低迷期から脱却しつつあることを受け、現在および今後の入札サイクルにおいて、契約運賃の大幅な引き上げが見込まれると予想している。厳格な規制",
    "s_ko": "나이트-스위프트 트랜스포테이션은 화물 시장이 약 4년간의 침체기를 벗어나면서, 현재 및 향후 입찰 기간 동안 계약 요금이 크게 인상될 것으로 전망하고 있습니다. 엄격한 규제 ",
    "so": "yahoo.finance",
    "url": "https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/knight-swift-says-shippers-already-152915175.html",
    "time": "2026-04-23T15:29:15+00:00",
    "rank": 1776958155.0,
    "content": "Knight-Swift Transportation anticipates significant contractual rate hikes during the current and upcoming bid cycles as the freight market emerges from a nearly four-year downturn. Strict regulatory enforcement and the recent fuel price shock are driving non-compliant and underperforming operators out of the market. Even without a notable pickup in demand, supply constraints have been severe enough to force shippers to contemplate realignment with asset-based carriers providing meaningful scale.\nThe Phoenix-based company’s CEO, Adam Miller, told analysts on a Wednesday quarterly call that mini-bid activity is increasing as shipper routing guides fail. He said some carriers are no longer honoring rates negotiated just one or two months ago and that some of its customers are already looking to lock up peak-season capacity. After capturing mid-single-digit contractual rate increases in its truckload business to start the year, the company is now eyeing high-single- to low-double-digit increases on the remaining 70% of its book.\n“I don’t think we’ve ever really seen the pressure on capacity … coming from regulatory forces versus just normal economics,” Miller said. “I think we could see more capacity coming out of the network than we typically would see in a cycle, and I feel like that could be a catalyst to really drive a strong bid season this year [and] also into next year.”\nSONAR: Outbound Tender Rejection Index (OTRI.USA) for 2026 (blue shaded area), 2025 (yellow line), 2024 (green line) and 2023 (pink line). A proxy for truck capacity, the tender rejection index shows the number of loads being rejected by carriers. Current tender rejections show a tightened truckload market.\nTo learn more about SONAR,\nclick here\n.\nSONAR: Van Contract Rate Per Mile Index (VCRPM1.USA) for 2026 (blue shaded area), 2025 (yellow line),\n2024 (green line) and 2023 (pink line).\nThe index shows a 7-day moving average of the initial reporting of dry van rate contract rates (without fuel or accessorial charges).\nKnight-Swift (\nNYSE: KNX\n) reported a headline net loss of $1.3 million, or 1 cent per share, for the first quarter. Adjusted earnings per share of 9 cents were in line with the\nnegative earnings revision\nthe company provided last week. Analysts were expecting adjusted EPS of 25 cents heading into earnings season.\nAdjusted EPS included several nonrecurring items. Headwinds included: 8 cents per share from a negative less-than-truckload claim development, 5 to 6 cents per share from weather and fuel headwinds, and 2 cents per share from an adverse value-added-tax ruling in its Mexico business. A roughly $8 million decline in net interest expense largely offset a similar decline in gains on equipment sales during the period.\nThe company reiterated its second-quarter adjusted EPS guidance range of 45 to 49 cents, which it had also provided last week.\nTable: Knight-Swift’s key performance indicators – Consolidated\nTruckload revenue was flat y/y at $1.05 billion,...",
    "content_source": "full"
  },
