  {
    "id": "8fcbf379c9ad",
    "cat": "finance",
    "title_en": "US to ‘shoot and kill’ Iranian boats laying mines in Hormuz, Trump says",
    "title_zh": "川普表示，美國將對在霍爾木茲海峽布設水雷的伊朗船隻「開火擊沉」",
    "title_zcn": "特朗普称，美国将对在霍尔木兹海峡布雷的伊朗船只“开火击沉”",
    "title_ja": "トランプ氏、ホルムズ海峡で機雷を敷設するイランの船に対し「撃沈する」と表明",
    "title_ko": "트럼프 대통령, 호르무즈 해협에서 기뢰를 설치하는 이란 선박에 대해 ‘사살’하겠다고 밝혀",
    "s_en": "US says it intercepted another tanker carrying Iranian oil as Trump underscores alleged infighting within Iran&#039;s leadership.",
    "s_zh": "美國表示已攔截另一艘載有伊朗石油的油輪，同時川普強調伊朗領導層內部據稱存在內鬥。",
    "s_zcn": "美国称拦截了另一艘载有伊朗石油的油轮，与此同时，特朗普强调了伊朗领导层内部据称存在的内斗。",
    "s_ja": "米国は、イラン産原油を積んだ別のタンカーを拿捕したと発表し、トランプ大統領はイラン指導部内の対立説を強調した。",
    "s_ko": "미국은 이란산 원유를 실은 또 다른 유조선을 나포했다고 밝혔으며, 트럼프 대통령은 이란 지도부 내부의 내분 의혹을 재차 강조했다.",
    "so": "aljazeera.com",
    "url": "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/4/23/us-to-shoot-and-kill-iranian-boats-laying-mines-in-hormuz-trump-says?traffic_source=rss",
    "time": "2026-04-23T14:58:30+00:00",
    "rank": 1776956310.0,
    "content": "President\nDonald Trump\nhas said he ordered the United States Navy to “shoot and kill” any Iranian boat laying mines in the Strait of Hormuz, a move that could jeopardise the fragile ceasefire between the two countries.\nThe US president also said on Thursday that the military will heighten its efforts to remove explosives from the strategic waterway.\nRecommended Stories\nlist of 3 items\nend of list\n“I have ordered the United States Navy to shoot and kill any boat, small boats though they may be (Their naval ships are ALL, 159 of them, at the bottom of the sea!), that is putting mines in the waters of the Strait of Hormuz. There is to be no hesitation,” Trump wrote in a social media post.\n“Additionally, our mine ‘sweepers’ are clearing\nthe Strait\nright now. I am hereby ordering that activity to continue, but at a tripled-up level!”\nIranian officials have repeatedly promised that their country would defend itself and respond to any US attack.\nHormuz – which had been open without interruption before the war – has emerged as a major point of contention in this war.\nIran closed down the strait in response to the US-Israeli military campaign, and it is now suggesting that it has rights to the passage that links the Gulf to the Indian Ocean – parts of which go through Iranian territorial waters.\nThe\nclosure of Hormuz has spiked oil prices, putting political pressure on Trump at home in the US,\nwhere the price\nof one gallon (3.8 litres) of petrol has surpassed $4,\nup from $3 before the conflict.\nA satellite image shows a fleet of small boats at sea, north of the Strait of Hormuz near the Kargan coast, Iran, April 22 [File: European Union/Copernicus Sentinel-2/Handout via Reuters]\nDueling blockades\nAbout 20 percent of the world’s oil and natural gas flowed through Hormuz before the war.\nAfter a two-week ceasefire came into effect last month, Trump announced a naval siege on Iranian ports and kept it in place even after Tehran announced\nreopening Hormuz\nin response to the inclusion of Lebanon in the truce.\nIran has set lifting the blockade as a precondition for resuming talks with the US.\nTrump extended the ceasefire that was set to expire on Wednesday, but Washington has kept its blockade on Iran-linked ships.\nThe Pentagon said on Thursday that the US military conducted a “maritime interdiction and right-of-visit” to a tanker carrying Iranian oil in the Indian Ocean.\nEarlier this week, the US military also said it seized an Iranian vessel and ordered dozens of others to turn around.\nMeanwhile, Iran\nhas also captured\nforeign commercial vessels around the Hormuz Strait, which it said were in violation of naval regulations.\nThe duelling blockades risk re-igniting the war. The US has not set a deadline for the extended truce.\nThe White House said on Wednesday that Trump is “satisfied”\nwith the siege\non Iran.\nTrump says Hormuz ‘sealed up tight’\nAlthough Iran has all but halted vessel traffic in the waterway, Trump said on Thursday that the US has “total control...",
    "content_source": "full"
  },
  {
    "id": "a97277597bb5",
    "cat": "finance",
    "title_en": "Warner Bros shareholders approve Paramount's $111bn takeover",
    "title_zh": "華納兄弟股東批准派拉蒙以1,110億美元收購該公司",
    "title_zcn": "华纳兄弟股东批准派拉蒙1110亿美元的收购案",
    "title_ja": "ワーナー・ブラザースの株主が、パラマウントによる1,110億ドルの買収案を承認",
    "title_ko": "워너브라더스 주주들, 파라마운트의 1,110억 달러 규모 인수안 승인",
    "s_en": "The approval came as Donald Trump is to attend a dinner with billionaire Paramount backers the Ellisons.",
    "s_zh": "這項批准正值唐納德·川普即將出席與派拉蒙影業的億萬富豪投資人艾利森夫婦共進晚餐之際。",
    "s_zcn": "就在这一批准消息传出之际，唐纳德·特朗普即将出席一场晚宴，与派拉蒙的亿万富翁支持者埃利森夫妇共进晚餐。",
    "s_ja": "この承認は、ドナルド・トランプ氏が、パラマウントの億万長者であるエリソン夫妻との夕食会に出席する予定である中で下された。",
    "s_ko": "이번 승인은 도널드 트럼프가 파라마운트의 억만장자 후원자인 엘리슨 부부와 만찬을 가질 예정인 가운데 이루어졌다.",
    "so": "bbc.com",
    "url": "https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cgj09ny0dq6o?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss",
    "time": "2026-04-23T14:55:21+00:00",
    "rank": 1776956121.0,
    "content": "In April, more than 1,400, including Emma Thompson, Ben Stiller and Javier Bardem, signed a letter warning of its impact.",
    "content_source": "full"
  },
  {
    "id": "95ceec117963",
    "cat": "chip",
    "title_en": "UK spy agency releases malware-blocking gadget for HDMI and DisplayPort cables — SilentGlass blocks malicious traffic traveling between display and computer",
    "title_zh": "英國情報機構推出適用於 HDMI 和 DisplayPort 線材的惡意軟體攔截裝置 — SilentGlass 可阻擋在顯示器與電腦之間傳輸的惡意流量",
    "title_zcn": "英国情报机构推出一款用于HDMI和DisplayPort线缆的恶意软件拦截设备——SilentGlass可拦截显示器与计算机之间传输的恶意流量",
    "title_ja": "英国の諜報機関が、HDMIおよびDisplayPortケーブル用のマルウェア遮断デバイスを公開――「SilentGlass」はディスプレイとコンピューター間でやり取りされる悪意のある通信を遮断する",
    "title_ko": "영국 정보기관, HDMI 및 DisplayPort 케이블용 악성코드 차단 기기 출시 — ‘SilentGlass’는 디스플레이와 컴퓨터 간에 전송되는 악성 트래픽을 차단한다",
    "s_en": "The NCSC, a part of the British GCHQ, has deployed this protective gadget throughout various government estates and is now making it publicly available through Goldilock Labs.",
    "s_zh": "隸屬於英國政府通信總部（GCHQ）的國家網絡安全中心（NCSC），已在各政府機構廣泛部署此防護裝置，並現透過 Goldilock Labs 向公眾開放。",
    "s_zcn": "隶属于英国政府通信总部（GCHQ）的国家网络安全中心（NCSC）已在多个政府机构内部署了这款防护设备，并正通过Goldilock Labs向公众提供该设备。",
    "s_ja": "英国のGCHQ傘下にあるNCSCは、このセキュリティ機器を政府の各施設に導入しており、現在はGoldilock Labsを通じて一般に公開している。",
    "s_ko": "영국 정부통신본부(GCHQ) 산하 기관인 NCSC는 이 보안 장치를 여러 정부 청사에 배치했으며, 현재 골디락 랩스(Goldilock Labs)를 통해 일반에 공개하고 있다.",
    "so": "tomshardware.com",
    "url": "https://www.tomshardware.com/tech-industry/cyber-security/uk-spy-agency-releases-malware-blocking-gadget-for-hdmi-and-displayport-cables-silentglass-blocks-malicious-traffic-traveling-between-display-and-computer",
    "time": "2026-04-23T14:52:23+00:00",
    "rank": 1776955943.0,
    "content": "The UK’s Government Communications Headquarters (GCHQ), a counterpart to the U.S.’s National\nSecurity\nAgency (NSA), just launched SilentGlass through the National Cyber Security Center (NCSC). This little gadget was announced during CYBERUK, a government-sponsored cyber security conference, and is designed to block malicious traffic traveling between a display and a PC. According to the\nNCSC\n, it built and designed this plug-and-play device to protect government estates and has been “approved for use in the most high-threat environments.”\nThe government has since licensed the design to Goldilock Labs, a UK-based cybersecurity firm that specializes in hardware that automatically cuts physical connections during a cyberattack, limiting potential damage to a network. It has partnered with\nSony\nUK Technology Center to make the product available globally, although the firm has yet to put the product publicly available on the market.\n“Display screens and monitors are everywhere in modern business environments, and the SilentGlass device will help protect previously vulnerable IT infrastructure with unprecedented ease,” NCSC Chief Technology Officer Ollie Whitehouse said, “Its development and commercialization show the impact that the NCSC can have, alongside industry partners, with an affordable and effective product now globally available.” Goldilock Labs co-founder Stephen Kines also said, “SilentGlass addresses a gap that has been widely overlooked. The hardware interfaces people rely on every day have rarely been treated as security boundaries, despite being exposed to risk through supply chains, third-party servicing, and direct physical access.”\nArticle continues below\nWhile SilentGlass is an interesting security device, some information security experts question the actual need for it. Cybersecurity expert Scott McGready said on\nX\n, “Can anyone genuinely tell me what risk this is addressing or is it a solution in search of a problem?” After all, most common cyberattacks do not use video signals as an attack vector. Nevertheless, that does not mean that it’s impossible to take advantage of HDMI and DisplayPort to exfiltrate information.\nWay back in 2020, a research paper revealed a technique which subtly\nchanged monitor brightness to steal data\nfrom air-gapped PCs, while a more recent study showed that\nAI can use signals leaking from HDMI cables\nto reconstruct what the target computer is displaying. These aren’t likely problems for the billions of home and office computers around the globe, as these techniques are complicated and would often cost more to deploy than the potential data they can gather from the average civilian.\nHowever, these vulnerabilities could be potential weak links in the security of government agencies and defense companies that deal with sensitive information. This makes them targets for nation-states who have the means and resources to use these attack vectors. The UK government has reportedly deployed this little gadget...",
    "content_source": "full"
  },
  {
    "id": "1866cbd72eb9",
    "cat": "finance",
    "title_en": "Why are FIFA World Cup 2026 tickets so expensive?",
    "title_zh": "為什麼 2026 年 FIFA 世界盃的門票這麼貴？",
    "title_zcn": "为什么2026年国际足联世界杯的门票这么贵？",
    "title_ja": "なぜ2026年FIFAワールドカップのチケットはこんなに高いのでしょうか？",
    "title_ko": "2026년 FIFA 월드컵 티켓은 왜 이렇게 비싼 걸까요?",
    "s_en": "Fans are critical of FIFA&#039;s pricing of tickets, accusing the world body of pricing them out of the global tournament.",
    "s_zh": "球迷對國際足總的票價定價提出批評，指責這家國際組織將他們排除在這項全球性賽事之外。",
    "s_zcn": "球迷们对国际足联的票价政策提出批评，指责这一国际组织将他们排除在这项全球性赛事之外。",
    "s_ja": "ファンはFIFAのチケット価格設定に批判的であり、この国際機関が世界的な大会から彼らを締め出していると非難している。",
    "s_ko": "팬들은 FIFA의 티켓 가격 책정 방식을 비판하며, 이 국제 기구가 가격을 너무 높게 책정해 팬들이 이 세계적인 대회를 관람할 기회를 박탈하고 있다고 비난하고 있다.",
    "so": "aljazeera.com",
    "url": "https://www.aljazeera.com/sports/2026/4/23/why-are-fifa-world-cup-2026-tickets-so-expensive?traffic_source=rss",
    "time": "2026-04-23T14:29:23+00:00",
    "rank": 1776954563.0,
    "content": "FIFA’s decision to release the latest tranche of World Cup tickets, coinciding with the 50-day countdown mark for the tournament, has left fans more frustrated than excited in advance of the biggest sporting event in the world.\nFootball’s global governing body\nannounced\nyet another “last-minute ticket phase” on Wednesday, with tickets for all 104 matches available on a first-come, first-served basis. Tickets are available in the three previously open categories, as well as the new “front category” pricing it added this month.\nRecommended Stories\nlist of 3 items\nend of list\nFans have expressed\noutrage\nat the exorbitant prices for the matches — the most expensive ticket for the final costs nearly $11,000 — since the first phase of ticket sales in December, and the latest round has left them wondering if FIFA’s “dynamic ticketing” is to be blamed for the pricing and availability of seats at the most sought-after sports event.\nHere’s what we know about the ticket prices for the World Cup cohosted by Canada, Mexico and the United States:\nWhy has FIFA reopened World Cup ticket sales?\nOstensibly, FIFA has plenty of unsold tickets in the bank despite its four previous sales windows, and it wants those tickets to sell out between now and the match days.\nThe global body has repeatedly claimed that the “cumulative attendance record of 3.5 million” set at the 1994 edition of the World Cup, which was hosted by the US, is on course to be surpassed during this year’s competition, but an unplanned fifth phase of ticket sales seems to suggest otherwise.\nThe unexpected release has raised questions about FIFA’s ticket sales strategy, as it previously said the April 1 phase was “the fourth and final” one that would remain open until the end of the competition.\nHowever, in a comment to Al Jazeera, a FIFA spokesperson said: “This ticket drop is part of the ongoing last-minute sales phase, which runs until the end of the tournament and allows the general public to purchase tickets via FIFA.com/tickets on a first-come, first-served basis.”\n“Along with this set of tickets, additional tickets will continue to be released to the public on an ongoing basis up until the final on Sunday, 19 July (subject to availability),” the spokesperson told Al Jazeera.\nWhy is FIFA struggling to sell tickets?\nThe most obvious answer would be that fans are not buying tickets, likely because they are significantly more expensive than promised.\nLast month, Football Supporters Europe (FSE)\nsaid\nthe North American bid had initially promised that tickets would be available from as little as $21. Instead, the cheapest tickets to go on sale — for $60 — have been limited. These tickets are allocated to a small portion of tournament venues and were introduced in a new pricing tier in December due to the immediate backlash over high pricing.\nFIFA has brushed aside suggestions that a lack of interest and “pricing out” are to be blamed for low sales.\n“Ticket sales for the FIFA World Cup remain strong...",
    "content_source": "full"
  },
  {
    "id": "4363440a211f",
    "cat": "finance",
    "title_en": "How Iran war has triggered soaring cost of medicines",
    "title_zh": "伊朗戰爭如何導致藥價飆升",
    "title_zcn": "伊朗战争如何导致药品价格飙升",
    "title_ja": "イランとの戦争が医薬品価格の高騰を招いた経緯",
    "title_ko": "이란 전쟁이 의약품 가격 급등을 촉발한 방식",
    "s_en": "Pharmacists in some countries have seen the cost of painkillers more than quadruple.",
    "s_zh": "部分國家的藥劑師發現，止痛藥的價格已飆升至原先的四倍以上。",
    "s_zcn": "一些国家的药剂师发现，止痛药的价格已上涨了四倍多。",
    "s_ja": "一部の国では、薬剤師が鎮痛剤の価格が4倍以上に跳ね上がっているのを目の当たりにしている。",
    "s_ko": "일부 국가의 약사들은 진통제 가격이 4배 이상 급등하는 것을 목격했다.",
    "so": "aljazeera.com",
    "url": "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/4/23/how-iran-war-has-triggered-soaring-cost-of-medicines-condoms?traffic_source=rss",
    "time": "2026-04-23T14:07:21+00:00",
    "rank": 1776953241.0,
    "content": "The United States and Israel’s war on Iran has pushed up the price of nearly everything.\nIn the early days of the war, the global supply of oil, gas and fertilisers was the main focus of this crisis.\nRecommended Stories\nlist of 3 items\nend of list\nIn recent days, however, pharmacists have also noted a spike in the price of medicines and contraceptives like condoms, as a result of the war. In the United Kindom, for example, pharmacies are charging 20 to 30 percent more for over-the-counter medicines, and the common painkiller paracetamol has more than quadrupled in price. In India, chemists are reporting price rises of common painkillers of as much as 96 percent.\nWe break down the reason behind the rise in prices and how badly countries around the world will be affected:\nWhy has the price of medicines increased?\nSince the early days of the war, Iran has blocked the Strait of Hormuz, through which 20 percent of the world’s oil and liquefied natural gas (LNG) supplies are shipped in peacetime. Experts say this has also disrupted pharmaceutical supply chains, which are reliant on the oil supply.\n“Pharmaceuticals are tied to both petrochemical feedstocks, a large part of which are sourced through the Persian Gulf,” Frederic Schneider, a nonresident senior fellow at the Middle East Council on Global Affairs, told Al Jazeera.\n“Furthermore, some logistics routes, including for pharmaceuticals, for example, between East Asia and Europe, have important sea and air transhipment stops in the Gulf, particularly in Dubai. These routes are especially fragile because many pharmaceuticals need special handling, including an unbroken cold chain. Both have been disrupted through the war,” he added.\nWouter Dewulf, a professor at the University of Antwerp in Belgium and an expert in pharma logistics, warned that while pharmaceutical supply chains are not in immediate danger, medicines are highly exposed to air logistics.\nThe US-Israel war on Iran has caused severe disruption for airlines, featuring widespread cancellations, airspace closures and a looming\njet fuel crisis\n.\n“35 percent of pharmaceuticals move by air, and about 90 percent of critical or life-saving pharmaceuticals and vaccines do so too. I estimate that 22 percent of global air cargo flows are exposed to Middle East disruptions,” he said.\n“So the main global effect for now is delays, rerouting, and higher costs, rather than a worldwide physical shortage.\n“There might be some modest price increases on pharmaceuticals, because of the increase in air cargo fares, mainly on the east-west corridors. For generic medicines, where the margins are much thinner, the relative increase in price might be higher,” he added.\nWhich pharma products have become expensive?\nPharmacies in the UK and India have noted an increase in the price of paracetamol, a drug commonly used to treat headaches and the flu.\n“Paracetamol is rising by approximately 96 percent,” a former board member of the Visakha Chemists Association in...",
    "content_source": "full"
  },
  {
    "id": "b3a9ac1b8393",
    "cat": "tech",
    "title_en": "Nebula sparkles in new Hubble snapshot | Space photo of the day for April 23, 2026",
    "title_zh": "星雲在哈伯望遠鏡的新影像中熠熠生輝 | 2026年4月23日太空每日一圖",
    "title_zcn": "哈勃新照片中星云熠熠生辉 | 2026年4月23日“每日太空照片”",
    "title_ja": "ハッブル宇宙望遠鏡の最新画像に映るきらめく星雲 | 2026年4月23日の「今日の宇宙写真」",
    "title_ko": "허블 우주 망원경이 포착한 반짝이는 성운 | 2026년 4월 23일 오늘의 우주 사진",
    "s_en": "Hubble revisits the Trifid Nebula in a spectacular image, revealing it's expansive splendor.",
    "s_zh": "哈伯太空望遠鏡以一張壯觀的影像再次捕捉三葉星雲，展現其遼闊的壯麗景象。",
    "s_zcn": "哈勃望远镜通过一张壮观的图像再次捕捉到了三叶星云，展现了它恢弘壮丽的景象。",
    "s_ja": "ハッブル宇宙望遠鏡がトリフィッド星雲を再び捉えた壮観な画像は、その広大で壮麗な姿を明らかにしている。",
    "s_ko": "허블 우주망원경이 트리피드 성운을 다시 포착한 장엄한 이미지를 통해, 그 광활한 장관을 드러내고 있다.",
    "so": "space.com",
    "url": "https://www.space.com/astronomy/hubble-space-telescope/nebula-sparkles-in-new-hubble-snapshot-space-photo-of-the-day-for-april-23-2026",
    "time": "2026-04-23T14:00:00+00:00",
    "rank": 1776952800.0,
    "content": "This image of the Trifid Nebula was captured by the Hubble Space Telescope 29 years after the telescope first imaged the nebula in 1997.\n(Image credit: NASA, ESA, STScI; Image Processing: Joseph DePasquale (STScI))\nA new image captured by the Hubble Space Telescope shows a spectacular nebula in all its glory. (And yes, it does kind of look like a cosmic sea slug.)\nNearly 30 years ago, Hubble looked at the Trifid Nebula. To celebrate the upcoming 36th anniversary of the telescope's launch on April 24, it looked at the nebula once again. And the image it captured is breathtaking.\nWhat is it?\nThe Trifid Nebula, more formally known as Messier 20, is a star-forming region located about 5,000 light-years away.\nArticle continues below\nThe\nHubble Space Telescope\nfirst looked at this nebula about 29 years ago in 1997. In looking at the nebula again all these years later, Hubble can show us how the nebula itself has changed over time, but it can also reveal new details as Hubble's camera has improved since taking its original image. During the\nspace shuttle mission STS-125\nin 2009, a of astronauts installed a better camera on Hubble with a wider field of view and improved sensitivity.\nWhy is it incredible?\nWhile this is a massive cloud of dust and gas where stars are created, in this new image, the nebula looks a bit like a sea slug, some have pointed out.\nIn the image, the nebula has a \"body\" made out of dust and gas and even a \"horn\" or \"antenna\" that is actually part of a plasma jet ejected by a young protostar in the nebula.\nBreaking space news, the latest updates on rocket launches, skywatching events and more!",
    "content_source": "full"
  },
  {
