    "id": "86909426fcc5",
    "cat": "chip",
    "title_en": "You can now run Linux on your ancient Windows 95 desktop with a new tool — very old Windows PCs, back to Intel 486, can cooperatively run very modern Linux kernels with WSL9x",
    "title_zh": "現在，您可以透過一款新工具，在您那台古老的 Windows 95 桌上型電腦上運行 Linux —— 即使是極為老舊的 Windows 電腦（甚至可追溯至 Intel 486 時代），也能透過 WSL9x 與最新的 Linux 核心協同運作",
    "title_zcn": "现在，借助一款新工具，你可以在那台古老的 Windows 95 台式机上运行 Linux 了——即使是老旧的 Windows 电脑（甚至可以追溯到 Intel 486 时代），也能借助 WSL9x 协同运行最新的 Linux 内核。",
    "title_ja": "新しいツールを使えば、古びたWindows 95デスクトップでもLinuxを実行できるようになりました。Intel 486時代まで遡る非常に古いWindows PCでも、WSL9xを利用すれば最新のLinuxカーネルを共存させて実行できます。",
    "title_ko": "이제 새로운 도구를 사용하면 오래된 Windows 95 데스크톱에서도 리눅스를 실행할 수 있습니다. 인텔 486 프로세서 시절의 아주 오래된 Windows PC에서도 WSL9x를 통해 최신 리눅스 커널을 함께 실행할 수 있습니다.",
    "s_en": "WSL9x enables users to run the most modern Linux kernels in Microsoft OSes as old as Windows 95.",
    "s_zh": "WSL9x 讓使用者能在舊至 Windows 95 的 Microsoft 作業系統上執行最新的 Linux 核心。",
    "s_zcn": "WSL9x 允许用户在包括 Windows 95 在内的早期微软操作系统上运行最新的 Linux 内核。",
    "s_ja": "WSL9x を使用すれば、Windows 95 といった古い Microsoft OS でも、最新の Linux カーネルを実行できるようになります。",
    "s_ko": "WSL9x를 사용하면 Windows 95와 같은 구형 Microsoft 운영 체제에서도 최신 Linux 커널을 실행할 수 있습니다.",
    "so": "tomshardware.com",
    "url": "https://www.tomshardware.com/software/operating-systems/get-linux-on-your-ancient-486-windows-95-desktop-using-wsl9x-very-old-windows-pcs-can-cooperatively-run-very-modern-linux-kernels",
    "time": "2026-04-23T12:22:14+00:00",
    "rank": 1776946934.0,
    "content": "A computer tinkerer and hacker has posted a tool called\nWSL9x\non Codeberg and taken to social media to boast that it might be “one of my greatest hacks of all time.” Hailey shared\na summary of WSL9x on Mastodon\n, referring to it by its longer and more meaningful name, the Windows 9x Subsystem for Linux. Oftentimes, folks like to run old OSes inside their modern ones, but WSL9x turns that on its head, as it can run the most modern Linux kernels within some of the earliest versions of Windows. It works on systems sporting\nWindows 95\nor newer, and even machines with 486 CPUs.\nIn her brief summary of WSL9x, Hailey highlights that the tool can “can run all your favorite Windows and Linux apps side-by-side with a modern Linux kernel running cooperatively with the Windows kernel in ring 0.” Moreover, it is even compatible with processors as far back as the 486, because no hardware virtualization is used. That contrasts with modern WSL in\nMicrosoft\n's latest versions of Windows.\nWe can see from the more detailed Codeberg readme and repository that there are three main components to WSL9x. These are a patched\nLinux kernel\n, a VxD driver, and wsl.com. The tinkerer and coder explained that “wsl.com is just a client program, it exists to hold a DOS window open for the console driver in the kernel to push chars into. + It also handles shuttling keystrokes from DOS to the console driver on IRQ.”\nArticle continues below\nWith the tool built and run, following the guide at Codeberg, users will be able to run “a modern Linux kernel (6.19 at time of writing) cooperatively inside the Windows 9x kernel, enabling users to take advantage of the full suite of capabilities of both operating systems at the same time, including paging, memory protection, and pre-emptive scheduling,” writes Hailey. No reboots are required to fire this up and get your favorite Windows 9X and Linux apps running side-by-side, highlights the developer.\nIn an age of AI and vibe coding, readers may also be refreshed to hear that WSL9x was “proudly written without AI.” Hailey also reveals that WSL9x has been brewing for six years, ever since she finished her\ndoslinux\nproject.\nMeanwhile, Linux is saying goodbye to the 486\nEarlier this month, we reported on Linux kernel devs starting to\nremove support for the 37-year-old Intel 486 CPU\n. Linus Torvalds had previously telegraphed that there was 'zero real reason' to continue support for this ancient processor.\nDeveloper Ingo Molnar will probably go down in history as the 486 on Linux gallowsman, though. Molnar authored a patch “that initially gets rid of the CONFIG_M486SX, CONFIG_M486, and CONFIG_MELAN Kconfig build option.” This patch is expected to be merged into Linux 7.1, so from that time, users won’t be able to build an i486 kernel image. Time to upgrade to a\nPentium\n, perhaps.\nGet Tom's Hardware's best news and in-depth reviews, straight to your inbox.\nFollow\nTom's Hardware on Google News\n, or\nadd us as a preferred source\n, to get our latest...",
    "content_source": "full"
  },
  {
    "id": "6f086cc4ce2a",
    "cat": "chip",
    "title_en": "More than 30,000 Samsung union members take to the streets to demand an average bonus of $400,000 per worker — May 21 strike date looms, union points to rival SK hynix granting higher bonuses to its employees",
    "title_zh": "超過 3 萬名三星工會成員走上街頭，要求每位員工平均獲得 40 萬美元的獎金——5 月 21 日的罷工日期迫在眉睫，工會指出競爭對手 SK 海力士已向其員工發放更高額的獎金",
    "title_zcn": "超过3万名三星工会成员走上街头，要求每位员工平均获得40万美元的奖金——5月21日的罢工日期临近，工会指出竞争对手SK海力士已向其员工发放了更高的奖金",
    "title_ja": "サムスンの組合員3万人以上が街頭へ繰り出し、従業員1人あたり平均40万ドルの賞与を要求――5月21日のストライキが迫る中、組合はライバル企業のSKハイニックスが従業員により高額な賞与を支給していることを指摘している",
    "title_ko": "3만 명 이상의 삼성 노조원들이 근로자 1인당 평균 40만 달러의 상여금을 요구하며 거리로 나섰다. 5월 21일 파업이 임박한 가운데, 노조는 경쟁사인 SK하이닉스가 직원들에게 더 많은 상여금을 지급하고 있다고 지적했다.",
    "s_en": "Workers at Samsung's largest chip fab staged a rally today, demanding higher pay and bonuses, comparing their compensation to what SK hynix offers its people.",
    "s_zh": "三星最大晶片廠的員工今天舉行集會，要求提高薪資與獎金，並將自身的薪酬待遇與SK海力士提供的待遇相比較。",
    "s_zcn": "三星最大芯片工厂的员工今天举行了集会，要求提高工资和奖金，并将他们的薪酬与SK海力士提供的待遇进行了对比。",
    "s_ja": "サムスンの最大規模の半導体工場では本日、従業員らが賃上げと賞与の増額を求め、SKハイニックスが従業員に提供している待遇と比較しながらデモを行った。",
    "s_ko": "삼성 최대 규모의 반도체 공장에서 일하는 근로자들이 오늘 집회를 열고, SK하이닉스가 직원들에게 제공하는 보상과 비교하며 임금 인상과 상여금 증액을 요구했다.",
    "so": "tomshardware.com",
    "url": "https://www.tomshardware.com/tech-industry/big-tech/more-than-30-000-samsung-union-members-take-to-the-streets-to-demand-an-average-bonus-of-usd400-000-per-worker-may-21-strike-date-looms-union-points-to-rival-sk-hynix-granting-higher-bonuses-to-its-employees",
    "time": "2026-04-23T12:09:03+00:00",
    "rank": 1776946143.0,
    "content": "Thousands of Samsung workers took to the streets today outside the company’s main chip fab, demanding a greater share of AI profits. According to the police, some 30,000 people attended the rally in Pyeongtaek, South Korea, more than 30 miles south of Seoul, while organizers claimed that over 39,000 were present.\nBloomberg\nreports that the Samsung labor union wants 15% of the company’s operating profit to be shared with chip-division workers and to remove the 50% bonus cap, as well as a 7% increase in pay. If this bonus is approved, that would amount to $27 billion (more than KRW 40 trillion), averaging more than $400,000 per worker.\nHowever, it seems that this might be a bit too much for Samsung management. It made a counteroffer of a 10% allocation of operating profit to bonuses, a 6.2% wage increase, and additional benefits like preferential mortgage loans. The union has apparently rejected this proposal, pointing out that rival SK hynix has allocated 10% of its annual operating profit for performance bonuses and also removed the maximum bonus limit for its workers. The Samsung workers argue that their bonuses only equate to less than 30% of what comparable SK hynix workers get.\nWhile Samsung has\nfallen behind its homegrown rival\nwhen it came to HBM3 dominance, it has since caught up after it became the first company to deliver next-generation HBM4 chips. “The company has spoken of crisis every year,” Samsung labor union head Choi Seung-ho told the publication. “But in the midst of those crises, it was not management that sustained Samsung Electronics. It was the employees here — the union members — who made the company the world’s leading semiconductor producer, who manufactured, improved processes, worked through the night, and raised yields.”\nArticle continues below\nIf the two parties fail to resolve the issue, the union says it will conduct an 18-day general strike starting May 21. This massive number of workers walking out of the posts will cause massive disruption for the company, with\nTradingKey\nestimating losses of around US$20.3 billion (around KRW 20 trillion). “Samsung will continue to make efforts to reach a swift agreement in wage negotiations,” a company spokesperson told\nBloomberg\n.\nFollow\nTom's Hardware on Google News\n, or\nadd us as a preferred source\n, to get our latest news, analysis, & reviews in your feeds.\nGet Tom's Hardware's best news and in-depth reviews, straight to your inbox.",
    "content_source": "full"
  },
  {
    "id": "2f3fb683f222",
    "cat": "tech",
    "title_en": "Our recommended choice as the best beginner mirrorless camera has $400 off, and has just hit its best price of the year at Best Buy",
    "title_zh": "我們推薦的最佳入門無反相機現正減價 400 美元，並在百思買（Best Buy）創下今年來最低價",
    "title_zcn": "我们推荐的最佳入门级无反相机现降价400美元，在百思买刚刚创下今年以来的最低价",
    "title_ja": "初心者向けミラーレスカメラとして当サイトがおすすめするモデルが400ドル値引きされており、ベストバイでは今年最安値を記録しました",
    "title_ko": "초보자에게 가장 추천하는 미러리스 카메라가 400달러 할인된 가격에 판매 중이며, 베스트바이에서 올해 최저가를 기록했습니다.",
    "s_en": "Expert tester Kimberley Lane rated the Sony A7C II as a perfect camera for enthusiasts, which produced impressive astrophotography results without breaking the bank.",
    "s_zh": "專業測試員金柏莉・萊恩（Kimberley Lane）將 Sony A7C II 評為一款專為攝影愛好者打造的完美相機，它能拍出令人驚豔的天文攝影作品，且價格親民。",
    "s_zcn": "专业评测员金伯利·莱恩认为，索尼A7C II是发烧友的理想之选，它能拍出令人惊叹的天文摄影作品，且价格亲民。",
    "s_ja": "専門のテスターであるキンバリー・レーンは、ソニーA7C IIを愛好家にとって理想的なカメラと評価し、手頃な価格で素晴らしい天体写真の結果をもたらすと述べた。",
    "s_ko": "전문 리뷰어 킴벌리 레인은 소니 A7C II를 애호가들에게 안성맞춤인 카메라로 평가하며, 부담 없는 가격으로 인상적인 천체 사진 결과물을 만들어낸다고 전했다.",
    "so": "space.com",
    "url": "https://www.space.com/technology/our-recommended-choice-as-the-best-beginner-mirrorless-camera-has-usd400-off-and-has-just-hit-its-best-price-of-the-year-at-best-buy",
    "time": "2026-04-23T12:00:00+00:00",
    "rank": 1776945600.0,
    "content": "When it comes to the\nbest mirrorless cameras\n, there is a huge choice from the world's leading photography brands. Our camera experts here at Space have tried and tested nearly all the\nbest cameras for astrophotography\nfrom Canon, Nikon and of course Sony, who are renowned for their advanced mirrorless camera systems.\nThe\nSony A1 II\nis the brand's top-of-the-line mirrorless camera with a professional-level spec and a price to match, but its sibling, the\nSony Alpha 7C II, is currently available for just $2,098 at Best Buy.\nThe\nSony A7C II\nperformed well for astro and it can autofocus down to -4EV, but added it's not a dedicated astro camera. However, if you want the all-around performance and occasionally dabble in astro, the Sony will easily have you covered.\nIt's the best price this full-frame mirrorless camera has been since April last year, and with a huge $400 off, it's an attractive purchase to anyone looking for a first full-frame mirrorless camera that is capable of\nshooting astrophotography\nin a lightweight, travel-friendly ultra-compact body.\nThis camera deal on Amazon is marked as a limited-time deal, but there's no indication of when it actually ends, so we'd say grab it while you can. It's worth noting that Adorama and Walmart are matching the same price, but only on the Black and Silver version, and it's also showing as unavailable on Amazon.\nPaul Brett is a deals writer at Space, Live Science, and across the Sports and Knowledge titles at Future. Paul is an award-winning photographer, having won the Mountain Photographer of the Year title at Trail Magazine. A huge fan of photography and cameras, he can be found on top of Scotland's mountains, wild camping, waiting to capture the Northern Lights or a cloud inversion.\nImage 1 of 4\nKimberley Lane recommended the Sony A7C II as brilliant first-time mirrorless camera.\n(Image credit: Kimberley Lane)\nThe Sony A7C II is lightweight and compact, so ideal for shooting on the move.\n(Image credit: Kimberley Lane)\nLane marked the Sony A7C II down for only having one memory card slot.\n(Image credit: Kimberley Lane)\nLane highlighted the Sony's fully-articulating screen as a review highlight.\n(Image credit: Kimberley Lane)\nThe Sony A7C II is our choice as the best entry-level full-frame camera, and our expert camera tester Kimberley Lane scored it with an impressive 4 out of 5-star rating in her\nSony A7C II review\n.\nLane was happy to recommend the A7C II as a superbly performing all-rounder. If you're looking to invest in your first full-frame camera or you're a beginner, this is a fantastic camera that is more than capable of delivering impressive images and video.\nThe Sony A7C II bridges the gap between Sony's portable APS-C cameras and its professional-grade full-frame bodies. It is designed for hybrid creators, both photographers and videographers, who want high-end performance in a travel-friendly form, which makes it ideal if you're\nnew to shooting astrophotography\nin dark sky areas and do...",
    "content_source": "full"
  },
  {
    "id": "ac1e864aeecc",
    "cat": "tech",
    "title_en": "Making contact with ET? Aliens may already know we're here",
    "title_zh": "與外星人接觸？外星人可能早已知道我們的存在",
    "title_zcn": "与外星人建立联系？外星人可能早已知道我们的存在",
    "title_ja": "地球外生命体との接触？　宇宙人はすでに私たちの存在を知っているかもしれない",
    "title_ko": "외계인과 접촉할 수 있을까? 외계인들은 이미 우리가 여기 있다는 사실을 알고 있을지도 모른다",
    "s_en": "Earth is dotted with many humongous, human-made structures. To an alien eye, they may be tell-tale signs of intelligent goings-on, betraying our existence and hinting at our capabilities.",
    "s_zh": "地球上散佈著許多龐大的人造結構。在外星人的眼中，這些或許正是智慧生命活動的明顯跡象，不僅暴露了我們的存在，更暗示了我們的能力。",
    "s_zcn": "地球上遍布着许多庞大的人造建筑。在外星人的眼中，这些建筑或许是智能生命活动的明显迹象，不仅暴露了我们的存在，也暗示了我们的能力。",
    "s_ja": "地球には、人間が作り出した巨大な建造物が数多く点在している。宇宙人の目には、それらは知性ある生命体の活動の明らかな証拠として映り、私たちの存在を露呈させ、その能力をほのめかすものとなるかもしれない。",
    "s_ko": "지구 곳곳에는 인간이 만든 거대한 구조물들이 즐비하다. 외계인의 눈에는 이 구조물들이 지능적인 생명체의 활동 흔적으로 보일 수 있으며, 우리의 존재를 드러내고 우리의 능력을 암시할 수도 있다.",
    "so": "space.com",
    "url": "https://www.space.com/space-exploration/search-for-life/making-contact-with-et-aliens-may-already-know-were-here",
    "time": "2026-04-23T12:00:00+00:00",
    "rank": 1776945600.0,
    "content": "We may already be signaling other intelligences beyond our solar system, without even trying.\nKunyu City, in the Xinjiang Uygur Autonomous Region of northwest China, hosts huge sprinklers that are irrigating over 1,317 acres (533 hectares) of winter wheat fields on the southern edge of the Taklamakan Desert. Then there's the world's largest cluster of\nsolar farms\n, a megaproject that covers 235 square miles (639 square kilometers) in Qinghai, China, high on the isolated Tibetan Plateau.\nAnd\nEarth\nis dotted with many other humongous, human-made structures like these. To an alien eye, they may be tell-tale signs of intelligent goings-on, betraying our existence and hinting at our capabilities.\nFarm fields in southern Poland as seen from space. In this region, narrow fields form a striped pattern rather than the large geometric shapes often seen elsewhere.\n(Image credit: NASA Earth Observatory image by Lauren Dauphin, using Landsat data from the U.S. Geological Survey)\nVisible signaling\nPeople who want to reach out to E.T. have long recognized the communication potential of such \"\nmegastructures\n.\" In the nineteenth-century, for example, multiple folks advanced proposals for broadcasting \"we're here\" messages via visible signaling.\nOne popular type of proposal involved displaying supposedly meaningful figures on parts of our planet that would be visible from the extraterrestrial target of choice.\nIn these plans, recalled\nDouglas Vakoch\n, president of Messaging Extraterrestrial Intelligence (METI) International in San Francisco, huge diagrams would be etched on large expanses of land here on Earth. For example, a visual representation of a right triangle could be shown, he said, with a square attached to each side of the triangle to illustrate diagrammatically the\nPythagorean theorem\n.\nBy clearing gargantuan stretches of forest, Vakoch said, such geometrical concepts could be seen by intelligent\naliens\nscanning the sunlit side of the Earth. This intended, symbolic representation of the Pythagorean theorem would be huge enough to be seen from\nthe moon\n— even by inhabitants of\nMars\n.\nBreaking space news, the latest updates on rocket launches, skywatching events and more!\nAnybody out there eyeing the Earth? This image of the massive galaxy cluster MACS J0416.1-2403 was part of the Hubble Space Telescope's Frontier Fields project.\n(Image credit: NASA, ESA, Pontificia Universidad Católica de Chile)\nHello, lunarians!\nVakoch said that among the early proponents of displaying pictures to communicate with extraterrestrials was the illustrious mathematician Karl Friedrich Gauss. In 1826, he was credited with suggesting such an approach for communicating with potential lunarians, inhabitants of Earth's moon.\n\"It was Gauss whose idea of inscribing the Pythagorean theorem in Siberian forests has often been touted as an early proposal for communicating with lunarians, although it's unclear whether Gauss actually said this, or whether it's only attributed to him,\"...",
    "content_source": "full"
  },
