    "id": "f9a4861fe474",
    "cat": "finance",
    "title_en": "In Tehran, money is short and a return to war looms over daily life",
    "title_zh": "在德黑蘭，資金短缺，而戰爭重燃的陰影籠罩著日常生活",
    "title_zcn": "在德黑兰，钱紧，战争阴云笼罩着日常生活",
    "title_ja": "テヘランでは資金が逼迫しており、日常生活には再び戦争の影が迫っている",
    "title_ko": "테헤란에서는 돈이 부족하고, 전쟁의 재개가 일상생활에 그림자를 드리우고 있다",
    "s_en": "The BBC's Lyse Doucet reports from Iran, where the buzz of busy shopping streets masks deep uncertainty over the country's future.",
    "s_zh": "BBC記者萊斯·杜塞特從伊朗發回報導，當地繁忙的購物街上人聲鼎沸，卻掩蓋了人們對國家未來深感不安的情緒。",
    "s_zcn": "BBC记者莱斯·杜塞特从伊朗发回报道，那里熙熙攘攘的商业街喧嚣声之下，掩盖着人们对国家未来深感不安的情绪。",
    "s_ja": "BBCのライズ・ドゥセ特派員がイランから報告する。活気あふれる商店街の喧騒の裏には、同国の将来に対する深い不安が潜んでいる。",
    "s_ko": "BBC의 리즈 두셋 기자가 이란 현장을 전합니다. 이곳에서는 분주한 쇼핑 거리의 활기찬 분위기 뒤에 이란의 미래에 대한 깊은 불확실성이 감춰져 있습니다.",
    "so": "bbc.com",
    "url": "https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cdrm8k7lzmko?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss",
    "time": "2026-04-23T11:26:01+00:00",
    "rank": 1776943561.0,
    "content": "Many women, young and old, no longer comply with laws dictating that they dress \"modestly\" and cover their heads, a legacy of the \"Women, Life, Freedom\" protests which swept Iran a few years ago - and like all protests, were crushed with lethal force.",
    "content_source": "full"
  },
  {
    "id": "60ccbb848b96",
    "cat": "chip",
    "title_en": "Bag a set of Razer Nommo 2.0 speakers for just $69 for a limited time — save $40 on new desktop speakers",
    "title_zh": "限時特惠，僅需 69 美元即可入手一套 Razer Nommo 2.0 喇叭——這款全新桌上型喇叭立省 40 美元",
    "title_zcn": "限时特惠：仅需 69 美元即可入手一套 Razer Nommo 2.0 音箱——这款全新台式音箱立省 40 美元",
    "title_ja": "期間限定で、Razer Nommo 2.0 スピーカーセットがわずか69ドルでお求めいただけます。新しいデスクトップスピーカーが40ドルお得です。",
    "title_ko": "한정 기간 동안 Razer Nommo 2.0 스피커 세트를 단 69달러에 만나보세요 — 새로운 데스크탑 스피커를 40달러 할인된 가격에 구매하세요",
    "s_en": "Bag a set of Razer Nommo 2.0 speakers for just $69. Save $40 on new desktop speakers at Woot",
    "s_zh": "只需 69 美元，即可入手一套 Razer Nommo 2.0 喇叭。在 Woot 購買新款桌上型喇叭，立省 40 美元",
    "s_zcn": "仅需 69 美元即可入手一套 Razer Nommo 2.0 音箱。在 Woot 购买新款台式音箱，立省 40 美元",
    "s_ja": "Razer Nommo 2.0 スピーカーセットがたったの69ドルで手に入ります。Wootで新しいデスクトップスピーカーを40ドルお得に購入しましょう",
    "s_ko": "Razer Nommo 2.0 스피커 세트를 단돈 69달러에 만나보세요. Woot에서 신형 데스크톱 스피커를 40달러 할인된 가격에 구매하세요",
    "so": "tomshardware.com",
    "url": "https://www.tomshardware.com/speakers/bag-a-set-of-razer-nommo-2-0-speakers-for-just-usd69-for-a-limited-time-save-usd40-on-new-desktop-speakers",
    "time": "2026-04-23T11:23:27+00:00",
    "rank": 1776943407.0,
    "content": "Are you looking out for a little set of desktop PC speakers on a tight budget? If so, you may be interested in this latest Woot offer that brings the price of a set of\nRazer Nommo 2.0 speakers to a bargain $69.99\n. This saves you a substantial $40 off the original $109.99 price tag. Razer is well known for making PC peripherals, which include speakers, keyboards, headsets, and, of course, mice. Razer products often command high prices, especially direct from Razer, but there are some deals to be found from other retailers that stock Razer products.\n●\nGrab this deal at Woot\nThe Razer Nommo speakers are a simple 2.0 configuration, with no added subwoofer, so don't expect a tsunami of bass. But this can be a good thing, especially if you're going to be using these speakers in an environment that doesn't need to hear thumping sub-bass rumbling through the property. Making a small set of speakers like this is ideal for some PC or console gaming in the bedroom, or even a dorm room at college, where you want to limit disturbances.\nThe speakers themselves are attractive little cans hoisted on small stands with 3\" woven glass fiber drivers mounted in the front and a bass port at the rear, to add a little kick to the bass frequencies. Volume and bass controls are mounted on the right speaker's stand and let you pump the bass (as much as you can on a 2.0 set of speakers) with its automatic gain control. These are older Razer speakers and have been replaced by newer models on the Razer store, which is one of the reasons these speakers are much cheaper now.\nA downside to these speakers for PC use is a lack of USB connectivity. You need to connect these Razer Nommo speakers to your PC via a 3.5mm to 3.5mm cable to an appropriate audio port on either the rear IO of your motherboard or the headphone jack of your PC's case. Yes, there are newer variants of these speakers, including the Razer Nommo V2 2.1, which comes with a subwoofer and is our pick for the\nbest 2.1 gaming speakers\n. But for just $69.99, these speakers are a great little deal, while stocks last, or time runs out on this limited Woot offer.\nIf you're looking for more savings, check out our\nBest PC Hardware deals\nfor a range of products, or dive\ndeeper\ninto\nour\nspecialized\nSSD and Storage Deals,\nHard Drive Deals\n,\nGaming Monitor Deals\n,\nGraphics Card Deals\n,\nGaming Chair\n,\nBest Wi-Fi Routers\n,\nBest Motherboard,\nor\nCPU Deals\npages\n.",
    "content_source": "full"
  },
  {
    "id": "48679eebaf9e",
    "cat": "chip",
    "title_en": "U.S. Commerce Secretary says Nvidia still hasn't sold any H200 AI GPUs to China — Chinese government is blocking imports in an attempt to push domestic semiconductor industry",
    "title_zh": "美國商務部長表示，Nvidia 至今仍未向中國出售任何 H200 AI 圖形處理器——中國政府正透過禁止進口來推動國內半導體產業發展",
    "title_zcn": "美国商务部长表示，英伟达至今尚未向中国出售任何H200人工智能GPU——中国政府正通过限制进口来推动国内半导体产业发展",
    "title_ja": "米商務長官は、Nvidiaが依然として中国にH200 AI GPUを1台も販売していないと述べた。中国政府は、国内の半導体産業を育成するため、輸入を阻止している。",
    "title_ko": "미국 상무부 장관은 엔비디아가 아직 중국에 H200 AI GPU를 단 한 대도 판매하지 않았다고 밝혔으며, 중국 정부는 자국 반도체 산업을 육성하기 위해 수입을 차단하고 있다고 전했다.",
    "s_en": "U.S. Commerce Secretary Howard Lutnick says Nvidia still hasn't sold a single H200 AI GPU to China, despite the ban being lifted four months ago. The Chinese government is making it difficult for Chin",
    "s_zh": "美國商務部長霍華德·盧特尼克表示，儘管禁令已於四個月前解除，但英偉達至今仍未向中國售出一顆H200人工智慧圖形處理器。中國政府正設法阻撓中國",
    "s_zcn": "美国商务部长霍华德·卢特尼克表示，尽管禁令已于四个月前解除，英伟达至今仍未向中国出售过任何一款H200人工智能GPU。中国政府正给中国企业制造障碍",
    "s_ja": "ハワード・ラトニック米商務長官は、4ヶ月前に禁輸措置が解除されたにもかかわらず、NVIDIAは依然として中国にH200 AI GPUを1台も販売していないと述べた。中国政府は、中国企業による",
    "s_ko": "하워드 루트닉 미국 상무장관은 4개월 전 금수 조치가 해제되었음에도 불구하고 엔비디아가 아직 중국에 H200 AI GPU를 단 한 대도 판매하지 않았다고 밝혔다. 중국 정부는 중국 기업들의",
    "so": "tomshardware.com",
    "url": "https://www.tomshardware.com/tech-industry/u-s-commerce-secretary-says-nvidia-still-hasnt-sold-any-h200-ai-gpus-to-china-chinese-government-is-blocking-imports-in-an-attempt-to-push-domestic-semiconductor-industry",
    "time": "2026-04-23T10:40:00+00:00",
    "rank": 1776940800.0,
    "content": "It's been four months since President Donald Trump lifted the ban on Nvidia selling its H200 AI chips to China, but Commerce Department Secretary Howard Lutnick says that the company still has yet to sell one to Chinese companies. According to\nReuters\n, Lutnick said Beijing is making it difficult for Chinese companies to get permission to import these chips, as the Chinese Communist Party is focused on supporting its domestic semiconductor industry.\nGo deeper with TH Premium: Taiwan, trade, and tariffs\n\"The Chinese central government has not let them, as of yet, buy the chips, because they’re trying to keep their investment focused on their own domestic industry,\" Lutnick said. \"We have not sold them chips as of yet.\"\nLutnick\nmade the same statement\nin late February during a House hearing, when asked about the status of H200 sales. However, Nvidia claimed that it\nalready received orders and export licenses\nfor multiple Chinese customers at GTC 2026 last month. These conflicting statements make the current situation unclear — especially as it’s also been reported that AI chip exports are bottlenecked at the Bureau of Industry and\nSecurity\n, where undersecretary Jeffrey Kessler has reportedly been\npersonally reviewing each individual application\n.\nThe U.S. is finally allowing Nvidia to export its chips to China again, with a 25% fee, and many major Chinese firms such as Alibaba and ByteDance were reportedly ready to order hundreds of thousands of Nvidia's AI GPUs. However, Beijing has called for its customs officials to block H200 imports and has essentially only allowed universities and R&D labs to acquire them. This is not surprising, as China has been pushing domestic companies to purchase locally-manufactured chips from Huawei, Alibaba, Baidu, Cambricon, Moore Threads, and others.\nThis is unwelcome news for Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang, as the company’s\nmarket share in China has fallen to under 60%\n— a big drop from the 95% share it had before the sanctions. Huang got into a\nheated discussion during a podcast\nwith Dwarkesh Patel, disagreeing with a total ban of AI chip exports to China and reiterating that the the U.S. government should not let Chinese AI chips dominate over U.S. manufacturers just to make it harder for Chinese researchers to build their own AI models on the U.S. tech stack.\nDespite the limitations and uncertainties, demand for H200 chips is still high in China — even though it’s behind the company’s latest Blackwell and upcoming Vera Rubin AI GPUs. It has gotten to the point that some firms are\nconsidering purchasing them on the black market.\nArticle continues below\nFollow\nTom's Hardware on Google News\n, or\nadd us as a preferred source\n, to get our latest news, analysis, & reviews in your feeds.\nGet Tom's Hardware's best news and in-depth reviews, straight to your inbox.",
    "content_source": "full"
  },
  {
    "id": "ed98eb7d20a4",
    "cat": "tech",
    "title_en": "2026 年「綜所稅六大新規」上路！信用卡、行動支付繳稅回饋一次看",
