    "time": "2026-04-23T10:08:43+00:00",
    "rank": 1776938923.0,
    "content": "弘塑今（\n23\n日）發布重訊，澄清媒體有關設備機台等關鍵技術流向中國的傳聞。對此，弘塑提出三點澄清，表示已針對侵害營業秘密之行為提起告訴，強調媒體報導屬不實揣測。\n弘塑表示，由於報導已造成公司名譽損害，因此依相關法令辦理澄清公告。該公司也提出三點表示，第一，公司高度重視智慧財產權、營業秘密及客戶資訊保護，亦已建置嚴謹的管理機制，全體員工，無論職位高低，均須遵守公司相關之規定。\n第二，針對報導之當事人，公司已就疑似侵害營業秘密之行為，依循法律途徑提起告訴，目前案件已進入司法偵查階段。基於偵查不公開原則，不便對外透露案件細節，但將全力配合檢調機關調查，以維護公司權益；第三，公司尚未發現有設備機台等關鍵機密技術流向中國之情事，針對媒體之報導，純屬不實揣測，故在此澄清說明。\n弘塑表示，除了公司主動發布（含新聞稿）或於公開資訊觀測站公告之訊息外，其餘資訊請投資人審慎判斷，以保障自身權益。\n弘塑今（\n23\n日）下跌\n7.35%\n至\n3,150\n元。高盛近期出具最新報告指出，弘塑今年營運主軸仍聚焦\nCoWoS\n先進封裝製程設備，但預期\nSoIC\n（系統級晶圓整合封裝）在\n2026-2028\n年將成為主要成長動能，估計屆時\nSoIC\n相關設備營收占比將超過\n50%\n，主要是因為\nCPO\n與未來世代的\nAI\n晶片將推動\nSoIC\n的採用更加廣泛。\n此外，由於技術複雜度極高，高盛預期\nSoIC\n與\nPL P\n設備的平均售價高達現行\nCoWoS\n設備的\n2\n倍與\n3\n倍，並調升弘塑\n2026\n年至\n2028\n年的預估獲利至\n36%\n，目標價從\n3,500\n元調升至\n4,500\n元。\n（首圖來源：\npixabay\n）\n延伸閱讀：",
    "content_source": "full"
  },
  {
    "id": "8fabaa771f01",
    "cat": "chip",
    "title_en": "Seagate FireCuda X Vault (8TB) review: A USB-powered, RGB-lit hard drive aimed at gamers",
    "title_zh": "Seagate FireCuda X Vault (8TB) 評測：專為遊戲玩家打造的 USB 供電 RGB 背光硬碟",
    "title_zcn": "希捷 FireCuda X Vault (8TB) 评测：一款专为游戏玩家打造的USB供电、RGB背光硬盘",
    "title_ja": "Seagate FireCuda X Vault (8TB) レビュー：ゲーマー向けのUSB給電式RGB照明搭載ハードドライブ",
    "title_ko": "시게이트 파이어쿠다 X 볼트(8TB) 리뷰: 게이머를 겨냥한 USB 전원 공급 방식의 RGB 조명 하드 드라이브",
    "s_en": "Seagate’s FireCuda X Vault is a gaming-focused 3.5-inch external drive with easily controlled RGB and a single USB-C cable for power and data.",
    "s_zh": "希捷的 FireCuda X Vault 是一款專為遊戲設計的 3.5 吋外接硬碟，具備可輕鬆控制的 RGB 燈效，並採用單一 USB-C 線纜同時傳輸電源與資料。",
    "s_zcn": "希捷的 FireCuda X Vault 是一款专为游戏设计的 3.5 英寸外置硬盘，配备可轻松控制的 RGB 灯效，并采用单根 USB-C 线缆同时传输数据和供电。",
    "s_ja": "シーゲートの「FireCuda X Vault」は、ゲーミング向けに設計された3.5インチの外付けドライブで、RGB照明を簡単に制御でき、電源とデータ転送の両方を1本のUSB-Cケーブルでまかなえます。",
    "s_ko": "시게이트의 FireCuda X Vault는 게이밍에 특화된 3.5인치 외장형 드라이브로, RGB 조명을 간편하게 제어할 수 있으며 전원 및 데이터 전송을 위한 USB-C 케이블이 하나로 통합되어 있습니다.",
    "so": "tomshardware.com",
    "url": "https://www.tomshardware.com/pc-components/external-ssds/seagate-firecuda-x-vault-8tb-review",
    "time": "2026-04-23T10:01:00+00:00",
    "rank": 1776938460.0,
    "content": "External 3.5-inch-based hard drives for backup and expanded storage have been common for decades (I brought one with me to college in 2000). But they typically required large laptop-style external power bricks, were often painfully slow, and were prone to random data-eating failure (ask me how I know).\nSeagate\n’s game-focused FireCuda X Vault drive (available in 8TB and 20TB options; we tested the 8TB) attempts to mitigate some of those past frustrations using a single USB-C connection that also powers the drive.\nIt’s also faster than portable hard drives (like the\nWD My Passport\nI tested in 2024), delivering a little under 200 MB/s writes in our real-world 50GB file transfer test. And if data loss concerns you, the FireCuda X Vault, like most Seagate drives, ships with two years of the company’s in-house Data Recovery Service. Of course, sub-200 MB/s speeds aren’t going to compete with even mid-range SSD these days, and at roughly 7.75x 2.1 x 5.25 inches and 2.75 pounds, it’s much larger than something like Sandisk’s solid-state\nDesk Drive (which I also tested at 8TB\n). But that 8TB desk-bound SSD is currently selling for $740, while Seagate’s 8TB spinning-platter Vault has an MSRP of $269. Is the Seagate Firecuda X Vault (which, apart from its built-in RGB, doesn’t look all that different from external 3.5-inch external drives I owned in the early 2000s) a smart storage option for gamers in 2026? Let’s walk through its features, put it through our\nexternal storage\ntesting, and find out if it deserves a spot on our list of the\nbest external hard drives and SSDs\n.\nSpecifications\nSwipe to scroll horizontally\nCapacity\n8TB\n20TB\nPrice\n$269\n$529\nDimensions\n7.8x 2.09 x 5.2 inches\n7.8x 2.09 x 5.2 inches\nWeight\n2.84 pounds\n2.84 pounds\nWarranty\n2 years\n2 years\nDesign and features of the Seagate FireCuda X Vault\n(Image credit: Tom's Hardware)\nThe Seagate FireCuda X Vault looks and feels a lot like any other external 3.5-inch external drive, perhaps with a bit more gamer edginess, thanks to some plastic slats designed to look like cooling fins and a wrap-around top surface with some cutouts to let the RGB shine through. The entire outer shell is plastic, save for a large foam pad on the bottom that’s there to prevent the drive sliding around on your desk (and also to hide the access screws underneath). The drive doesn't exactly scream premium storage, but it doesn’t feel or look cheap, either.\n(Image credit: Tom's Hardware)\nThe sole port, which is USB-C, is housed on the rear center. And because this is a bus-powered drive, you’ll need to use a port (and a cable) that’s capable of delivering 15W of power. That might mean plugging the drive into the back of your PC if you’re using a desktop. And considering most modern systems don’t have more than two or three native USB-C ports, you might have to pick up a powered USB-C hub if you have other peripherals that need those ports.\n(Image credit: Tom's Hardware)\nThe drive ships with a 0.5-meter (1.64 feet)...",
    "content_source": "full"
  },
  {
    "id": "529e7babc271",
    "cat": "chip",
    "title_en": "AI agent designs a complete RISC-V CPU from a 219-word spec sheet in just 12 hours — comparably simple design required 'many tens of billions of tokens'",
    "title_zh": "人工智慧代理僅花費 12 小時，便根據一份僅 219 字的規格書設計出一顆完整的 RISC-V 處理器——相較之下，同樣簡單的设计卻需要「數百億個字元」",
    "title_zcn": "人工智能代理仅用12小时，便根据一份仅219个单词的规格说明书设计出一款完整的RISC-V处理器——而类似的简单设计通常需要“数百亿个令牌”",
    "title_ja": "AIエージェントが、わずか12時間で219語の仕様書から完全なRISC-V CPUを設計した――これと同程度の単純な設計でも、通常は「数百億トークン」が必要とされる",
    "title_ko": "AI 에이전트가 단 12시간 만에 219단어로 된 사양서 하나로 완전한 RISC-V CPU를 설계해냈다. 이와 비슷한 수준의 단순한 설계에도 ‘수백억 개의 토큰’이 필요했던 것과 대비된다.",
    "s_en": "AI chip design startup Verkor.io claims that its agentic AI system, Design Conductor, has autonomously produced a complete RISC-V CPU core.",
    "s_zh": "人工智慧晶片設計新創公司 Verkor.io 宣稱，其代理式人工智慧系統「Design Conductor」已自主設計出一個完整的 RISC-V CPU 核心。",
    "s_zcn": "人工智能芯片设计初创公司Verkor.io宣称，其自主智能系统“Design Conductor”已自主设计出一个完整的RISC-V CPU内核。",
    "s_ja": "AIチップ設計のスタートアップ企業Verkor.ioは、同社のエージェント型AIシステム「Design Conductor」が、RISC-V CPUコアを自律的に設計したと発表している。",
    "s_ko": "AI 칩 설계 스타트업인 Verkor.io는 자사의 에이전트형 AI 시스템인 ‘Design Conductor’가 완전한 RISC-V CPU 코어를 독자적으로 설계해냈다고 밝혔다.",
    "so": "tomshardware.com",
    "url": "https://www.tomshardware.com/tech-industry/artificial-intelligence/ai-agent-designs-a-complete-risc-v-cpu-from-a-219-word-spec-in-just-12-hours",
    "time": "2026-04-23T10:00:00+00:00",
    "rank": 1776938400.0,
    "content": "AI chip design startup Verkor.io claims, in a\nresearch paper\npublished in March, that its agentic AI system, Design Conductor, autonomously produced a complete RISC-V CPU core — taking a 219-word requirements document and generating a verified, layout-ready design in 12 hours, which is orders of magnitude faster than the standard 18- to 36-month timelines seen in commercial chip design.\nGo deeper with TH Premium: AI and data centers\n(Image credit: Microsoft)\nThis is the first time an autonomous agent has built a working CPU from spec to GDSII layout file, according to Verkor. The resulting processor — VerCore — is a five-stage pipelined, in-order, single-issue core that met timing at 1.48 GHz on the ASAP7 7nm process design kit, scoring 3,261 on the CoreMark benchmark.\nVerkor’s paper goes into detail on the pipeline architecture, which includes instruction fetch, decode, execute, memory, and writeback stages with early branch resolution and operand forwarding.\nDuring optimization, the system independently implemented a fast Booth-Wallace multiplier that clocked at 2.57 GHz and a one-cycle branch penalty design that the agent selected after implementing and testing both one-cycle and two-cycle variants. Verkor compares VerCore's CoreMark performance to Intel's Celeron SU2300, a 2011 mobile chip based on the\nPenryn architecture\n.\nA five-stage in-order core with no caches and no out-of-order execution is a fairly straightforward design by industry standards. Verkor's own paper notes that leading-edge chips cost north of $400 million and take 18 to 36 months with engineering teams in the hundreds, but VerCore is far simpler than those designs. That said, the 12-hour timeline is still notable for a fully autonomous run from spec to layout, even if it did require \"many tens of billions of tokens\" at this comparatively pale level of complexity.\nArticle continues below\n(Image credit: Verkor.io)\nVerCore hasn’t been physically fabricated and was instead verified in simulation using Spike, a reference RISC-V ISA simulator, and ASAP7 is an academic process design kit, not a production 7nm node. Verkor says it can run a uCLinux variant in simulation.\nVerkor's paper is candid about the limitations of the underlying language models, admitting that the agent sometimes “underestimates the complexity of work that is required to address certain issues.” For example, in one case, when failing to meet timing, Design Conductor tried to make major changes to \"deepen the pipeline, instead of looking for simpler explanations.\"\nIn another case, the researchers observed the model reasoning about Verilog, an event-driven language, as if it were sequential code. \"While we found that this did not impact DC's ability to achieve functional correctness, it made it more challenging for DC to debug timing issues,\" the researchers explained.\nThe researchers estimate that five to 10 human experts will still be required to guide the system toward a production-ready chip. In...",
    "content_source": "full"
  },
  {
    "id": "bbfdb36c831b",
    "cat": "finance",
    "title_en": "Mortgage rates hit 'lowest level in the last three spring homebuying seasons': Mortgage and refinance interest rates today",
    "title_zh": "房貸利率創下「近三個春季購屋季以來的最低水準」：今日房貸與再融資利率",
    "title_zcn": "房贷利率创下“近三个春季购房季以来的最低水平”：今日房贷及再融资利率",
    "title_ja": "住宅ローン金利が「過去3回の春の住宅購入シーズンで最も低い水準」に：本日の住宅ローンおよび借り換え金利",
    "title_ko": "모기지 금리, ‘지난 3년 동안의 봄 주택 구매 시즌 중 최저 수준’ 기록: 오늘의 모기지 및 재융자 금리",
    "s_en": "Mortgage rates dipped below 6.3% for the first time in more than a month amid market optimism about ongoing negotiations between the U.S. and Iran.\nThe average 30-year mortgage was 6.23% through Wedne",
    "s_zh": "隨著市場對美伊持續談判持樂觀態度，房貸利率時隔一個多月後首次跌破6.3%。\n截至週三，30年期房貸平均利率為6.23%",
    "s_zcn": "随着市场对美伊持续谈判持乐观态度，抵押贷款利率时隔一个多月首次跌破6.3%。\n截至周三，30年期抵押贷款平均利率为6.23%",
    "s_ja": "米国とイランの間で続く交渉に対する市場の楽観的な見方を受け、住宅ローン金利は1カ月以上ぶりに6.3％を下回った。\n水曜日時点での30年固定金利住宅ローンの平均金利は6.23％だった。",
    "s_ko": "미국과 이란 간의 협상 진행에 대한 시장의 낙관론 속에 주택담보대출 금리가 한 달여 만에 처음으로 6.3% 아래로 떨어졌다.\n수요일까지 30년 만기 주택담보대출 평균 금리는 6.23%를 기록했다.",
    "so": "yahoo.finance",
    "url": "https://finance.yahoo.com/personal-finance/mortgages/article/mortgage-rates-hit-lowest-level-in-the-last-three-spring-homebuying-seasons-mortgage-and-refinance-interest-rates-today-100000199.html",
    "time": "2026-04-23T10:00:00+00:00",
    "rank": 1776938400.0,
    "content": "Mortgage rates dipped below 6.3% for the first time in more than a month amid market optimism about ongoing negotiations between the U.S. and Iran.\nThe average 30-year mortgage was 6.23% through Wednesday, down from 6.3% a week earlier, according to Freddie Mac data.\n“Rates currently stand at their lowest level in the last three spring homebuying seasons,” Sam Khater, Freddie Mac’s chief economist, said in a statement. “This improvement, coupled with a pickup in purchase applications and refinance activity, as well as an increase in monthly pending home sales, underscores signs of improving momentum in the market.”\nMortgage applications for home purchases surged 10% last week, according to the Mortgage Bankers Association, and refinancing applications were up 6%. Meanwhile, new listings rose 3% for the four weeks through April 19, according to Redfin. The brokerage called it a sign of a “small spring rebound.”\nHere are the current mortgage rates, according to the latest Zillow data:\n30-year fixed:\n6.10%\n20-year fixed:\n6.05%\n15-year fixed:\n5.56%\n5/1 ARM:\n6.20%\n7/1 ARM:\n5.99%\n30-year VA:\n5.60%\n15-year VA:\n5.23%\n5/1 VA:\n5.16%\nRemember, these are the national averages and rounded to the nearest hundredth.\nHere are 8 strategies for getting the lowest mortgage rate possible.\nHere are today's mortgage refinance interest rates, according to the latest Zillow data:\n30-year fixed:\n6.13%\n20-year fixed:\n6.16%\n15-year fixed:\n5.60%\n5/1 ARM:\n5.97%\n7/1 ARM:\n6.02%\n30-year VA:\n5.51%\n15-year VA:\n5.06%\n5/1 VA:\n5.42%\nAs with mortgage rates for purchase, these are national averages that we've rounded to the nearest hundredth. Refinance rates can be higher than purchase mortgage rates, but that isn't always the case.\nUse the mortgage calculator below to see how various mortgage rates will impact your monthly payments.\nYou can bookmark the Yahoo Finance\nmortgage payment calculator\nand keep it handy for future use, as you shop for homes and lenders. Be sure to use the dropdown to include private mortgage insurance costs and HOA dues if they apply to you. These monthly expenses, along with your mortgage principal and interest rate, will give you a realistic idea of what your monthly payment could be.\nA mortgage interest rate is the fee charged by a lender for borrowing money, expressed as a percentage. There are two basic types of mortgage rates: fixed and adjustable rates.\nA\nfixed-rate mortgage\nlocks in your rate for the entire life of your loan. For example, if you get a 30-year mortgage with a 6% interest rate, your rate will remain at 6% for the entire 30 years. (Unless you refinance or sell the home.)\nAn\nadjustable-rate mortgage\nkeeps your rate the same for the first few years, then changes it periodically. Let’s say you get a 5/1 ARM with an introductory rate of 6%. Your rate would be 6% for the first five years, and then the rate would increase or decrease once per year for the last 25 years of your term. Whether your rate goes up or down depends on several...",
    "content_source": "full"
  },
  {
    "id": "4b6704ad7627",
    "cat": "tech",
    "title_en": "'That's just not a winning strategy': Congress objects (again) to Trump's planned NASA budget cuts",
    "title_zh": "「這根本不是一項成功的策略」：國會（再次）反對川普擬議的NASA預算削減案",
    "title_zcn": "“这根本不是制胜策略”：国会（再次）反对特朗普计划削减NASA预算",
    "title_ja": "「それは勝てる戦略ではない」：議会がトランプ大統領のNASA予算削減案に（再び）反対",
    "title_ko": "“그건 결코 성공할 수 없는 전략입니다”: 의회, 트럼프 행정부의 NASA 예산 삭감 계획에 (다시 한번) 반대",
    "s_en": "Members of Congress from both sides of the aisle objected to President Trump's proposed NASA budget cuts during a House hearing on Wednesday (April 22).",
    "s_zh": "在週三（4月22日）的眾議院聽證會上，來自兩黨的國會議員均對川普總統提議削減美國太空總署（NASA）預算一事表示反對。",
    "s_zcn": "在周三（4月22日）的众议院听证会上，来自两党的国会议员均对特朗普总统提出的削减美国宇航局预算的提议表示反对。",
    "s_ja": "水曜日（4月22日）に行われた下院の公聴会で、与野党双方の議員が、トランプ大統領が提案したNASAの予算削減案に反対した。",
    "s_ko": "수요일(4월 22일) 열린 하원 청문회에서 여야 의원들은 트럼프 대통령이 제안한 NASA 예산 삭감안에 반대했다.",
    "so": "space.com",
    "url": "https://www.space.com/space-exploration/thats-just-not-a-winning-strategy-congress-objects-again-to-trumps-planned-nasa-budget-cuts",
    "time": "2026-04-23T10:00:00+00:00",
    "rank": 1776938400.0,
    "content": "President Trump's big NASA budget cuts appear to be dead on arrival, again.\nEarlier this month, the White House released its fiscal year (FY) 2027 federal budget request, which slashes\nNASA's total budget by 23%\nand its science funding by 47%.\nTrump proposed the\nsame basic reductions\nfor FY 2026 but was\ndenied by Congress\n, which has the power of the purse in Washington. And it looks like history will repeat itself this year.\nThe U.S. House of Representatives' Committee on Science, Space, and Technology held a hearing about the NASA budget on Wednesday (April 22) that featured agency chief\nJared Isaacman\nas its star witness.\nDuring the event, representatives from both sides of the aisle voiced concerns about the proposed cuts and signaled an intent to reject them again.\n\"Both the president and Congress have provided explicit direction for NASA to undertake a range of activities, from exploration and science to aeronautics research. We must ensure that NASA is funded at a level that allows it to pursue those missions,\" Rep. Brian Babin (R-Texas), who chairs the committee, said during the hearing.\n\"I simply do not believe that this budget proposal is capable of supporting what\nPresident Trump\nhimself has directed the agency to accomplish over the course of his two terms, nor what Congress has directed by law,\" he added.\nBreaking space news, the latest updates on rocket launches, skywatching events and more!\nBabin stressed that he's a fiscal conservative and is worried about the national debt (which currently stands at nearly $39 trillion). But pinching pennies on NASA doesn't make sense, he argued, given that the United States is facing increased\ncompetition in the final frontier from China\n.\nChina aims to put astronauts\non the moon by 2030\n, Babin pointed out, and\noperates a space station\nin low Earth orbit that will likely keep running long after the\nInternational Space Station\nis retired. The nation is also launching increasingly complex and ambitious robotic science missions.\n\"We must ask whether this proposed budget maintains United States civil and commercial space dominance, or if we risk ceding that leadership to our adversary, China,\" Babin said. \"Only through Congress, our commercial space sector and the administration working together can we ensure continued U.S. leadership in space.\"\nAn artist's rendering of a NASA Artemis moon base.\n(Image credit: NASA)\nThe committee's ranking member, Rep. Zoe Lofgren (D-California), also voiced strong objections.\n\"OMB, once again, tries to argue that NASA and the United States will continue to lead in space and\nEarth\nscience, human exploration, aeronautics and space technology, while all but exploration would see\ndraconian cuts\n,\" Lofgren said, referring to the White House's Office of Management and Budget.\n\"Cuts totaling 5.6 billion, or 23% from the fiscal year 2026 enacted level, [are] not wise. These reductions do not exactly send a 'welcome home' message to the\nArtemis 2\ncrew or to the NASA...",
    "content_source": "full"
  },
  {
    "id": "487df95fb499",
    "cat": "tech",
    "title_en": "Google 轉向代理式工作流程，執行長：75% 新程式碼已由 AI 產生",
    "title_zh": "Google 轉向代理式工作流程，執行長：75% 新程式碼已由 AI 產生",
    "title_zcn": "Google 轉向代理式工作流程，執行長：75% 新程式碼已由 AI 產生",
    "title_ja": "Googleがプロキシ型ワークフローへ移行、CEO「新規コードの75％はAIによって生成されている」",
    "title_ko": "구글, 에이전트 기반 워크플로로 전환… CEO “신규 코드 75%가 AI에 의해 생성됐다”",
    "s_en": "AI 模型和 agent 技術演進強化了編碼工具性能，有助於專案開發。Google 目前約 75% 新程式碼由 [&#8230;]",
    "s_zh": "AI 模型和 agent 技術演進強化了編碼工具性能，有助於專案開發。Google 目前約 75% 新程式碼由 [&#8230;]",
    "s_zcn": "AI 模型和 agent 技術演進強化了編碼工具性能，有助於專案開發。Google 目前約 75% 新程式碼由 [&#8230;]",
    "s_ja": "AIモデルとエージェント技術の進化により、コーディングツールの性能が向上し、プロジェクト開発に役立っています。現在、Googleの新規コードの約75％は[&#8230;]",
    "s_ko": "AI 모델과 에이전트 기술의 발전은 코딩 도구의 성능을 향상시켜 프로젝트 개발에 기여하고 있습니다. 현재 구글의 신규 코드 중 약 75%는 [&#8230;]",
    "so": "technews.tw",
    "url": "https://technews.tw/2026/04/23/75-percent-of-all-new-code-at-google-is-now-ai-generated-and-approved-by-engineers/",
    "time": "2026-04-23T09:49:52+00:00",
    "rank": 1776937792.0,
    "content": "AI 模型和 agent 技術演進強化了編碼工具性能，有助於專案開發。Google 目前約 75% 新程式碼由 AI 產生，比例持續攀升，轉向代理式工作流程以提升營運效率\n「Google 內部用 AI 產生程式碼已有一段時間了。如今，Google 75% 新程式碼由 AI 產生，並經過工程師審核通過」，Google 執行長皮查伊（Sundar Pichai）表示。\n這個數字近年來持續攀升，回顧 2024 年 10 月，Google 當時表示公司約有 25% 的程式碼由 AI 產生；到了 2025 年秋季，Google 則表示已上升至 50%。\nGoogle 一直推動員工運用 AI 進行編碼以及各式工作任務，隨著 Google Cloud Next 2026 大會揭幕，皮查伊表示 Google 正轉向「真正的代理式工作流程」，工程師指揮自主運作的「數位工作小組」，派遣各種 agent 去完成任務。\n「近期，一項由 agent 和工程師合作完成、特別複雜的程式碼遷移任務，其完成速度比一年前僅由工程師獨自執行快上 6 倍」，皮查伊補充說。\nGoogle 的工程師不僅使用自家模型產生程式碼，部分工程師更被設定使用 AI 的具體目標，並納入績效考核。值得一提的是，有工程師因業務需求，向公司申請使用競爭對手的模型，其中以 Claude Code 最受青睞，甚至因此在工程師之間造成一些緊張關係。\n除 Google 外，其他科技公司如微軟、Meta、Snap 同樣鼓勵多多運用 AI 進行編碼、處理工作任務\n2025 年 4 月，微軟執行長納德拉（Satya Nadella）曾表示，微軟某些專案的程式碼中，有 20% 至 30% 由 AI 撰寫。微軟技術長史考特（Kevin Scott）則認為，5 年內將會有 95% 程式碼由 AI 產生。\n外媒 Business Insider 取得一份 Meta 的文件顯示，截至 2025 年第四季，Meta 所設定的目標，要求部分團隊工程師提交程式碼變更，應有 55% 屬於 AI 協助的成果；旗下 Creation Org 訂下目標，在 2026 上半年 65% 的工程師，其提交的程式碼要有 75% 以上由 AI 工具輔助產生。另一方面，Snap 本月稍早表示，在全新營運模式下，至少有 65% 新程式碼將由 AI 產生。\n（首圖來源：shutterstock）",
    "content_source": "full"
  },
